DTX License
===========

DTX is a data format: a table of R rows and C columns, in one of the
variants doc/SPEC.md defines. This repository contains the specification,
the requirements it is written against, the terminology and glossary, and
the tests that keep the documents to one another.

The format may be implemented freely. doc/SPEC.md is the contract, and an
independent reader or writer owes only the acknowledgement below.

1. THE DOCUMENTS - doc/SPEC.md, doc/requirements.md, doc/terminology.md,
   doc/glossary.md and the rest under doc/ - are Copyright (c) 2026
   Robbert van Dalen.

2. THE READERS, WRITERS AND TESTS can be used freely within your own
   programs, for any platform, even for commercial releases. The only
   condition is that you must indicate somehow in your documentation that
   you have used DTX. They are everything under src/, go/, dotnet/ and
   68k/.

Attribution
-----------

* DTX, its specification and its tests are Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert van
  Dalen; written by Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code) under Robbert van
  Dalen's direction.
* ST4, the packer a DTX2 column is packed with, is a separate format
  specified at https://github.com/odipar/ST4 and Copyright (c) 2026
  Robbert van Dalen.
* src/main/java/org/st4 is a carried copy of that repository's packer, at
  odipar/ST4@498aa25 and not edited here, so a DTX2 file is written with
  no packer beside this one. ST4's own license puts its compressor under
  the BSD 3-Clause License, which is below, and this repository contains a
  copy of that compressor.
* go/internal/st4 is the same packer in Go, a carried copy of
  odipar/YMX@611e321's go/internal/st4, whose own package comment names
  the Java it is a port of. The package comment is edited here to name
  where the copy came from; no code is. beside.go and packer.go are DTX's
  own. The BSD 3-Clause License below covers it as it covers the Java.
* dotnet/nt4 is that same packer in C#, a carried copy of
  odipar/ST4@498aa25's csharp/src/Nt4, not edited here. The project builds
  it with the implicit usings its own tree builds it with. The BSD
  3-Clause License below covers it too.
* 68k/ST4_wrap.S is a carried copy of that repository's file, at
  odipar/ST4@02f3cc0, so a packaged DTX2 reader contains a decoder. ST4's
  license permits a decompressor to be used freely, on the one condition
  that your documentation indicates that you have used ZX1, via ST4.

